# Prefer Original Implementation

When addressing bugfixes or inconsistencies, start from the master / original
working code and fix based on that implementation.

The master is the existing working codebase being integrated: historical Library,
the host's original sources, or vanilla mk64 — whichever the current path came from.
Read that code first. Match its control flow, data flow, and side effects unless
something in it is fundamentally mistaken.

Do not invent a new codepath, helper, or parallel implementation to paper over a
bug. New paths complicate the tree and introduce bugs the original never had.

Only write a different approach when the original is clearly wrong for this tree
(wrong ABI, broken RAM contract, or a real logic error) — and say so in the
approval proposal, citing what is mistaken and why a new path is required.
